#=GF DR   SO; 0000205; three_prime_UTR;
#=GF DR   GO; 0006398; mRNA 3'-end processing by stem-loop binding and cleavage;
#=GF RN   [1]
#=GF RM   7899087
#=GF RT   The sequence of the stem and flanking sequences at the 3' end of histone
#=GF RT   mRNA are critical determinants for the binding of the stem-loop binding
#=GF RT   protein.
#=GF RA   Williams AS, Marzluff WF
#=GF RL   Nucleic Acids Res 1995;23:654-662.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   10571029
#=GF RT   Formation of the 3' end of histone mRNA.
#=GF RA   Dominski Z, Marzluff WF
#=GF RL   Gene 1999;239:1-14.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   17998288
#=GF RT   Early evolution of histone mRNA 3' end processing.
#=GF RA   Dávila López M, Samuelsson T
#=GF RL   RNA. 2008;14:1-10.
#=GF CC   The mRNAs of metazoan histone genes lack a poly-A tail. 3' end processing
#=GF CC   occurs at a site between a highly conserved stem-loop (modelled by this
#=GF CC   family) and a purine rich region around 20 nts downstream (the histone
#=GF CC   downstream element, or HDE). The stem-loop is bound by a 31 kDa stem-loop
#=GF CC   binding protein (SLBP - also termed the histone hairpin binding protein,
#=GF CC   or HBP). Together with U7 snRNA binding of the HDE, SLBP binding nucleate
#=GF CC   s the formation of the processing complex. The histone 3' UTR stem-loop is
#=GF CC   also involved in nucleocytoplasmic transport of the mRNA, and in stability
#=GF CC   regulation and translation efficiency in the cytoplasm.
#=GF WK   Histone_3'_UTR_stem-loop
#=GF SQ   46

